{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#468","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#468","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#468\",\"parent_revision\":\"ef211c82d8c07f10c7ed25a81535097a0d301105\",\"root_revision\":\"72a7c5935edbda26a0b82fdc4df01e0f2814e800cbee70760aa945d61efa5c24\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbacklog_core has no lifespan management. The GitHub client (`get_github()`) is instantiated per-call, which means token validation and connection setup are repeated on every tool invocation. Under load, this creates redundant API handshakes.\\n\\nFastMCP v3 provides a `@lifespan` decorator that runs setup once at server start and yields a context dict available via `ctx.lifespan_context`. This is the correct place to validate `GITHUB_TOKEN`, create the GitHub client, and fail fast if credentials are missing.\\n\\nFiles affected: `.claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py`, `.claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/github.py`\\n\\nWork required:\\n- Define a `@lifespan` that initializes the GitHub client and validates `GITHUB_TOKEN`\\n- Pass the `FastMCP` instance `lifespan=app_lifespan`\\n- Tools that use GitHub access `ctx.lifespan_context[\\\"github\\\"]` instead of calling `get_github()` per-request\\n- `GitHubUnavailableError` surfaces at startup rather than first GitHub call\\n\\nSource: FastMCP v3 docs `servers/lifespan.mdx` \u2014 `@lifespan` yields a dict into `ctx.lifespan_context`; compose multiple lifespans with `|` operator.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 `@lifespan` pattern verified | AVAILABLE | Item description cites `servers/lifespan.mdx` |\\n| 2 | `get_github()` call sites in server.py | DERIVABLE | Grep `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` for `get_github` |\\n| 3 | FastMCP version in use supports lifespan | DERIVABLE | Check pyproject.toml |\\n| 4 | Graceful degradation for no-token mode | MISSING | Policy decision: should server fail-fast or degrade gracefully? |\\n\\nVerdict: READY with one policy decision (fail-fast vs graceful degradation in no-token mode).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **add lifespan management to backlog_core for github client initialization** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill review of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Refactor. Medium complexity. Affects all tools that call get_github(). Low risk \u2014 behavior unchanged, only initialization point moves.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A `@lifespan` context manager defined in `server.py` or `github.py` validates `GITHUB_TOKEN` and creates the GitHub client at startup\\n- `FastMCP` instance passed `lifespan=app_lifespan`\\n- Tools that use GitHub access `ctx.lifespan_context['github']` instead of calling `get_github()` per-request\\n- `GitHubUnavailableError` or equivalent surfaces at server startup (fail-fast) rather than on first GitHub call\\n- Server still starts successfully in offline/no-token mode for read-only local operations (graceful degradation)\\n- Regression: all existing tool behaviors unchanged \u2014 only the initialization point changes\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add @lifespan, update tools to use ctx.lifespan_context\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 refactor get_github() for lifespan compatibility\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog MCP server, I need a `@lifespan` that initializes the GitHub client once at server start so token validation and connection setup are not repeated on every tool invocation under load.\\n\",\"digest\":\"1ed116a5ab4720ed962a1607bdbcbe69ef50157636bfb3195c61202755c4798f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg0rPQ\"}"}